# Running and verifying

> 🔴 **The smoke test is currently failing — 5 assertions, as of 2026-08-03.** You did
> not break it. Its assertions were written for the milestone 1 build and one of them
> literally reads *"cargo lost health with no enemies in the build"* while enemies now
> exist. Separately, the cargo dies at 3,882 px of the 8,900 px route. Read
> [docs/status.md](mdc:docs/status.md) before interpreting any failure, and do not
> "fix" the game to satisfy a stale assertion.

```sh
# Play.
Godot --path .

# End-to-end check: drives a whole run and asserts the result.
# Exits non-zero on failure, so it can gate a commit.
Godot --headless --fixed-fps 60 --path . res://tools/smoke_run.tscn

# Screenshots of nine game states, into user://screenshots.
# Must run windowed - saving a viewport image needs a real rendering device.
Godot --fixed-fps 60 --resolution 1280x720 --path . res://tools/screenshot_run.tscn

# Regenerate route control points after changing the road shape.
python3 tools/road_calc.py --target 9000 --wavelength 2800
```

On this machine the binary is
`/Applications/Godot.app/Contents/MacOS/Godot`.

## What the smoke test asserts

Route length 9000 px, run completes, terrain events in order
`Mud, Road, Mud, Road`, time on mud at the ×0.60 factor, the Fast level dominating
the speed accounting, and the full telemetry key set. **Adding a telemetry field
means updating `tools/smoke_run.gd` too**, or the key-set assertion fails.

It asserts the duration band this build can actually produce, which is not yet the
three-minute floor of §7 — see [docs/status.md](mdc:docs/status.md) for why that is
correct rather than a bug.

## Telemetry output

`user://telemetry`, which on macOS is
`~/Library/Application Support/Godot/app_userdata/MagicLogisticsInit`. One JSON per
run, named `run_<date>_P<profile>_seed<n>.json`, 31 keys.

## Standard of proof

An assertion is not a playtest. This project exists to evaluate **control feel**, so
"the smoke test passes" is not evidence that a control change is good. When a change
touches how the game feels, say so and ask for a play session rather than reporting
it as verified.

Report outcomes plainly: if the smoke test fails, paste the output. If you did not
run it, say you did not run it.
